  "description": "WESSUL crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C57 H70 N12 O23 Tb4,C1 H4 O1,3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.883-3.938 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 107.02-111.88°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb4L4(CO3)(acac)2(H2O)2(CH3OH)2]·3H2O·CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
